{
    name: "Stadestér (Cities)",
    open: false,
    "stadester": {
        name: "Cities/Settlements",
        type: "vector.points",
        unit: "Urban Population",
        icon: "location_city",
        description: [
            "### Stadestér",
            "A global historical database of 34.400+ cities and urban settlements from 3300BC to the present. Split by version (1.0, 1.1).",
            "",
            "Historical names, capital cities, and other visuals can be toggled in the **Mapmodes** menu.",
            "<details>",
            "<summary>Methodology (1.1)</summary>",
            "Recalculation of [Reba et al.](https://doi.org/10.1038/sdata.2016.34) using [Worldcitypop](https://www.worldcitypop.com/) as ground truth anchors. Relative rates of change were then assessed using Reba, and flagging systems for manual geolocation were put in place. Most cities were located using [Geohack](https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/GeoHack), [Google Places API](https://developers.google.com/maps/documentation/places/web-service/overview), and [Photon (OSM)](https://github.com/komoot/photon).",
            "",
            "In addition, historical names and capital city histories were added to Stadestér via agent chunking and batch processing. Spatiotemporal heuristics were then applied to flag chunks for review.",
            "",
            "Since **1.1** is an improvement on Stadestér **1.0**, we highly encourage you to read its [methodology report](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.17180328).",
            "</details>",
            "<details>",
            "<summary>Methodology (1.0)</summary>",
            "Merger of Buringh, Chandler, de Vries, GHSL (UCDB), GHS-POP, Modelski, Populstat, Reba et al. and Wikipedia. Cities were then geolocated using Google Maps/Nominatim. Population estimates were calculated via weighted geometric means of cubic spline interpolations over source domains.",
            "- Methodology report: [10.5281/zenodo.17180328](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.17180328)",
            "</details>"
        ],
        filepath: "${l_stad}/stadester_1.1.json",
        permissions: [
            "default"
        ],
        display_options: {
            bubble_size: 0.4,
            capital_color_mode: "state",
            capital_constant_color: "#FFDC00",
            color_mode: "growth",
            dataset: "stadester_1.1",
            filled: true,
            growth_palette: "Rainbow",
            halo: false,
            heuristic_culling: false,
            label_collision: true,
            large_city_contrast: 1.0,
            max_cities: 4000,
            min_pop: 0.01,
            mobile_heuristic_culling: true,
            opacity: 0.7,
            prefer_least_diacritics: true,
            show_capitals: true,
            show_capital_underlines: false,
            show_labels: true,
            skip_unknown_unicode: true,
            strip_parentheses: true
        },
        legend: {
            colourscheme: "Plasma",
            type: "pseudo-log",
            modes: [
                "population",
                "growth",
                "area",
                "density",
                "region"
            ]
        }
    }
}